/**
 * @page dev_stream_config SDR device stream configuration
 * 
 * @section creating_stream Creating stream
 * 
 * Once the SDR device parameter configuration is finished, a stream object must be created to begin streaming data. Stream is created via previously created device interface by invoking
 * @ref lime::SDRDevice::StreamCreate(const lime::StreamConfig&, uint8_t) "StreamCreate()" function. The stream parameters (packet size, PPS and etc.) must be set up beforehand using
 * @ref lime::StreamConfig "StreamConfig" structure. Example of stream creation:
 * 
 * @code{.cpp}
 * #include <iostream>
 * #include <vector>
 * #include <memory>
 * #include <limesuiteng/DeviceRegistry.h>
 * #include <limesuiteng/SDRDevice.h>
 * #include <limesuiteng/RFStream.h>
 * #include <limesuiteng/StreamConfig.h>
 * #include <limesuiteng/DeviceHandle.h>
 * #include <limesuiteng/SDRConfig.h>
 * #include <limesuiteng/ToString.h>
 * #include <limesuiteng/OpStatus.h>
 * 
 * int main()
 * {
 *    ... // SDR device discovery, registration and configuration
 * 
 *    uint8_t moduleIndex = 0;   // For SDR device with single RF chip
 *    
 *    // Setting up stream configuration
 *    lime::StreamConfig miniStreamConf = {};   // Stream configuration with default values
 *    std::unique_ptr<lime::RFStream> miniStream = device->StreamCreate(miniStreamConf, moduleIndex);
 * 
 *    ... // Other program code   
 *       
 *    lime::DeviceRegistry::freeDevice(device); // End of program code
 *    return 0;
 * }
 * @endcode
 * 
 * @section stream_parameters Stream parameters
 * 
 * @if RST_SUPPORT
 * @embedRstVerbatim{
 * .. admonition:: Note
 * 
 *    The declared names of stream parameters in the table below match the parameter names used within :cpp:enum:~lime::StreamConfig structure.
 * }
 * @else
 * @note The declared names of stream parameters in the table below match the parameter names used within @ref lime::StreamConfig "StreamConfig" structure.
 * @endif
 * 
 * Here is a detailed table of @ref lime::StreamConfig "StreamConfig" structure members with additional information about each parameter below the table:
 * <table>
 *    <tr>
 *       <th> Parameter </th>
 *       <th> Units/Options </th>
 *       <th> Default initialized value </th>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> samplesInPacket </td>
 *       <td> Sample count </td>
 *       <td> 0 </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> packetsInBatch </td>
 *       <td> Packet count </td>
 *       <td> 0 </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> format </td>
 *       <td> `I12` or `I16` or `F32` </td>
 *       <td> `I16` </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> linkFormat </td>
 *       <td> `I12` or `I16` </td>
 *       <td> `I16` </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> bufferSize </td>
 *       <td> Bytes </td>
 *       <td> 0 </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> channels </td>
 *       <td> Tx `[0 1]` and Rx `[0 1]` </td>
 *       <td> Tx `[]` and Rx `[]` </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> timestampType </td>
 *       <td> `SAMPLE_TICKS` or `REAL_SECONDS` or `UNIX_EPOCH` </td>
 *       <td> `SAMPLE_TICKS` </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> hintSampleRate </td>
 *       <td> Hz </td>
 *       <td> 0 </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> statusCallback </td>
 *       <td> - </td>
 *       <td> `nullptr` </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> userData </td>
 *       <td> - </td>
 *       <td> `nullptr` </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> usePoll </td>
 *       <td> `true` or `false` </td>
 *       <td> `true` </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> waitPPS </td>
 *       <td> `true` or `false` </td>
 *       <td> `false` </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> alignPhase </td>
 *       <td> `true` or `false` </td>
 *       <td> `false` </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> negateQ </td>
 *       <td> `true` or `false` </td>
 *       <td> `false` </td>
 *    </tr>
 * </table>
 * 
 * @subsection packet_size Packet size
 * 
 * The size of a single packet is defined by <b>samplesInPacket</b> parameter. The maximum number of samples for a single packet also depends on selected number of streaming channels (channels parameter)
 * and the size of a single sample (linkFormat parameter). For reference, a table with maximum packet sizes for different channel and sample size configurations is shown below the paragraph. 
 * 
 * <table>
 *    <tr>
 *       <th> Packet size, samples </th>
 *       <th> Channel count </th>
 *       <th> Single sample size, bytes </th>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> 1020 </td>
 *       <td> 1 </td>
 *       <td> 4 </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> 510 </td>
 *       <td> 2 </td>
 *       <td> 4 </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> 1360 </td>
 *       <td> 1 </td>
 *       <td> 3 </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> 680 </td>
 *       <td> 2 </td>
 *       <td> 3 </td>
 *    </tr>
 * </table>
 * 
 * Customization of packet size depends on the current device gateware. If the device gateware does not support variable packet sizes, the default packet size will always be set to one of the values shown in
 * the table above. If device gateware supports variable packet sizes, then the specified packet size will be applied. If the custom packet size is higher than the allowed maximum value, the packet size will
 * be clamped to the one of the maximum values (depending on your channels and linkFormat configuration). It is also important to note, that packet sizes must be aligned to packet data bus width. If the specified
 * packet size is not a multiple of bus width, then the packet size will be rounded down to the nearest packet size that is a multiple of the packet data bus width. Therefore, the specified custom packet size might be
 * different from the packet size that was anticipated initially.
 * 
 * If custom packet size is not important, you can set the <b>samplesInPacket</b> parameter to value <b>0</b>. The optimal packet size will be auto set when the streaming object is created or reconfigured by using
 * @ref lime::RFStream::Setup(const lime::StreamConfig&) "Setup()" function.
 * 
 * @subsection stream_batch Stream batch
 * 
 * A size of a single stream batch is defined by <b>packetsInBatch</b> parameter. If the stream batch parameter is set to value <b>0</b>, the batch size is auto calculated to fit into 100 us
 * Tx/Rx time slot. If the 100 us timeslot is not suffiecient, a custom stream batch value can be specified. The custom specified value will override the automatically calculated stream batch value.
 * If specified stream batch size is too large, it is clamped to the maximum possible value, which is determined by the size of dma buffer (it is dynamically allocated for each device) and packet size
 * ratio (MaxBatchSize = dmaBufferSize / packetSize). The smallest possible batch size is 1 packet.
 * 
 * @subsection hint_sample_rate Sample rate
 * 
 * Sample rate parameter is an optional parameter and can be provided as an additional hint to stream configuration. By default this parameter is initialized to value <b>0</b>. This allows the software to 
 * automatically retrieve the configured device sample rate and use it for internal calculations. If the software is unable to retrieve the configured device sample rate, you must manually set the sample
 * rate parameter to the exact value that was used in initial device configuration.
 */